\section*{Weeks 13--14: Contract Implementation Summary}

\subsection*{Planned Deliverables (from thesis plan)}

\begin{itemize}
    \item Develop SubscriptionManager.rs (state management, payments, verification)
    \item Implement PayPerView.rs (one-time access, tokens)
    \item Create PurchaseVerification.rs (ownership transfers, resale)
    \item Write unit tests (80\% coverage) and deploy to local testnet
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{What Was Actually Built}

The original plan envisioned three separate ink! smart contracts. Based on Phase 3 architecture decisions (RMRK 2.0 pallets abandoned, pallet-nfts adopted instead), the implementation was refactored into a \textbf{FRAME pallet + ink! contract} architecture:

\subsubsection*{1. pallet-content-rights (replaces all three planned contracts)}

\textbf{Location:} pallets/content-rights/

A unified FRAME pallet that handles all three access models through a single RightsType enum, backed by pallet-nfts for token storage:

\begin{table}[H]
\centering
\caption{Planned Contracts vs Pallet Implementation}
{\footnotesize
\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{lLL}
\toprule
\textbf{Planned Contract} & \textbf{Pallet Implementation} & \textbf{Key Extrinsics} \\
\midrule
SubscriptionManager.rs & RightsType::Subscription & register\_content, subscribe, renew\_subscription, check\_access \\
PayPerView.rs & RightsType::PayPerView & register\_content (with PPV price), pay\_per\_view, check\_access \\
PurchaseVerification.rs & RightsType::Ownership & register\_content, subscribe (permanent), transfer\_ownership, transfer\_ownership\_cross\_chain \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabularx}
}
\end{table}

\textbf{Relevant commits:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item 5d8ab9a --- Add pallet-nfts to runtime for content rights NFT layer
    \item 8b532b5 --- Add pallet-content-rights with full rights management and 23 unit tests
    \item 2a7962e --- Add ownership transfer extrinsics (local and cross-chain)
\end{itemize}

\subsubsection*{2. RightsManager ink! 6 Contract}

\textbf{Location:} contracts/rights-manager/

An ink! 6 smart contract that provides a higher-level API over the pallet, deployed on pallet-revive (PolkaVM):

\begin{itemize}
    \item mint\_content\_rights --- Creates a rights NFT for content
    \item check\_access --- Verifies access via custom precompile
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Relevant commits:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item f4bc50c --- Scaffold RightsManager ink! 6 contract
    \item 7bc9651 --- Add custom pallet-revive precompile for content rights read access
\end{itemize}

\subsubsection*{3. Unit Tests}

\textbf{23 unit tests} in pallets/content-rights/src/tests.rs covering:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Content registration (all three types)
    \item Subscription creation and renewal
    \item Pay-per-view access and counter tracking
    \item Ownership transfers (local and cross-chain)
    \item Expiry and access checks
    \item Error paths (unauthorized, not found, expired)
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Relevant commit:} 8b532b5

\subsubsection*{4. Local Testnet Deployment}

Deployed and verified on Zombienet local testnet:
\begin{itemize}
    \item 2-chain topology (Rococo relay + Content Rights parachain 100)
    \item Verified via scripts/verify-runtime-has-contracts.sh
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{Deviations from Plan}

\begin{table}[H]
\centering
\caption{Deviations from Plan}
{\footnotesize
\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{lLL}
\toprule
\textbf{Planned} & \textbf{Actual} & \textbf{Rationale} \\
\midrule
Three separate ink! contracts & One FRAME pallet + one ink! contract & FRAME pallets are more efficient for core state management; ink! provides the external API layer \\
ink! on pallet-contracts (WASM) & ink! 6 on pallet-revive (PolkaVM) & pallet-revive is the current Polkadot SDK direction; pallet-contracts is legacy \\
RMRK 2.0 for NFT nesting & pallet-nfts with attribute-based semantics & RMRK pallets abandoned and incompatible with current polkadot-sdk \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabularx}
}
\end{table}

